{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774028962,"nonce":"xNrZqGZt2Ey18SgzoCgeHupksU0=","title":"P1: Work-unit DB schema + .issue file + agent-commit auto-discovery","message":"Parent: f3dbb3e\n\nWork-unit table, .issue file written by wt, agent-commit auto-discovers from .issue file.\n\n## DB Migration\n- New table work_units: id, issue_id, repo_id, branch, parent_branch (derived from __ parsing), kind (leaf/integration/solo), state (open/committed/merged/abandoned), assigned_session_id, continuation TEXT, continuation_by TEXT, continuation_at INTEGER, created_at, activated_at (first commit), last_commit_at, resolved_at, auth_request_id\n- Index on (repo_id, branch), (repo_id, issue_id)\n\n## wt changes (~/.dotfiles/bin/wt)\n- Add optional --issue \u003cid\u003e flag (repeatable)\n- When present: write .issue file to worktree root containing issue ID(s), one per line\n- POST to Mandible: POST /api/work-units/claim { issue_id, branch, repo_id }\n- --no-issue flag for ad-hoc work (no .issue file, no registration)\n- If Mandible unreachable: still write .issue file locally, log warning, proceed\n\n## agent-commit changes (~/.dotfiles/bin/agent-commit)\n- Auto-discover issue from .issue file if --issue not provided: if [[ ${#issues[@]} -eq 0 \u0026\u0026 -f .issue ]]; then issues+=($(cat .issue)); fi\n- After commit, POST /api/work-units/activate { issue_id, branch, repo_id } to update activated_at and last_commit_at\n\n## dwt changes (~/.dotfiles/bin/dwt)\n- Before removing worktree: if branch has no unique commits and has a work unit, POST /api/work-units/release to set state back to open\n\nNOTE: wt, agent-commit, dwt are in the dotfiles repo (~/.dotfiles/bin/). Changes to those files require a feature branch in the dotfiles repo, not mandible.","files":null}]}